/**
 * @file badSrcIWithoutLoad.cnl
 *   Test case for linNet.\n
 * A current source has no load impedance connected. This leads to an linear equation
 * system with zero determinant. linNet doesn't abort the calculation but ends with an
 * infinite node potential.\n
 *   The Octave script is still generated but the transfer function object it creates,
 * would be bad an make Octave fail when used. linNet has placed an explaining error
 * message in the script to avoid a hard to understand, generic, nonspecific Octave error
 * message.
